, "timestamp_updated": 1336229988, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "1312063", "author": {"steamid": "76561197991204613", "personaname": "Scrivener", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Scrivener-Wraith/", "num_games_owned": 636, "num_reviews": 27, "playtime_forever": 2196, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1751, "last_played": 1656810567, "avatar": "4941a7cfc3620dcd7d3bc7b75046c85ec873c215"}, "language": "english", "review": "Incredibly fun game in spite of a few of it's failings. If there wasn't such a thing as a spectacle FPS before this and Bulletstorm then there certainly is now. The campaign clocks in somewhere around 7-10 hours, however during that time you drop onto a Orc Kruiser, Ride a train/battering Ram to a manufactorum, drop a titan weapon on orkz and far more things that if you're a fan of the 40K Franchise leaves you giddy the closer you get to the end. Multiplayer however, is a bit tacked on, however, they have managed to make something that is still fun to play with friends, and multiplayer has really come into it's own with the Horde Mode that was added post release. If you like being a god of war mary sue and cleaving through hundreds of enemies as just as big opponents charge towards you as well and you're a fan of 40K this is a definate buy.", "timestamp_created": 1336188467, "timestamp_updated": 1336188467, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": 